(D/'input-manifest.json').write_text(json.dumps(manifest,indent=2)+'\n')
base='''You are an independent rules-summary reader in a blind evaluation. Read ONLY these two rules-data files:\n{summary}\n{questions}\nDo not read authoritative rulebooks, extracted text, answer keys, manifests, earlier answers, grades, reviewer findings, other files, parent history or web links. Do not browse or use prior game knowledge. Do not communicate with other readers. Write ONLY {output}.\n\nUse only the frozen summary as rules authority. Scenario facts explicitly stated in a question are givens; do not reject hypothetical setup merely because it is not narrated in the summary. If a requested rule is absent, state which requested part is unsupported; never guess.\n\nTechnical delivery: load EACH allowed file by bounded contiguous character chunks, each at most 5000 characters, output cap at least 4000 tokens. Use a separate tool result for each chunk. Print filename, start/end character offsets, total characters, SHA256 of that chunk, and the exact full chunk. Read every chunk of BOTH files before answering. Do not rely on line counts, silent filesystem loading or cropped tool results. Preserve a delivery_receipt in the output listing all contiguous ranges, totals and file SHA256. If a tool output truncates, retrieve the affected range again in smaller pieces.\n\nFor every question independently: enumerate its own requested clauses; search the entire summary for every named item and relevant terms before declaring a rule absent; select the complete relevant operative units; then give concise direct rulings for each clause and actual calculated values in numeric cases. Self-check every clause against your selected passages. Context inherited by a table from its introduction/legend or earlier definition must be included when controlling the asked fact. Complete operative quotations can supply ordinary lookup facts; concrete scenarios still need direct conclusions/calculations.\n\nSource-unit integrity: choose complete heading-bounded leaf subsections or explicit unions of complete relevant paragraphs/lists, or a full relevant table row with header and governing context. A parent section includes its child subsections through the next same-or-higher heading. Do not select only its introduction when the rest controls the procedure. For tables compute row boundaries by actual newlines, keeping all cells through the final pipe; never arbitrary fixed-length snippets. For prose keep actual complete paragraph/list boundaries. Before saving, mechanically verify quotes exist verbatim in the frozen summary and are not cut midword/midcell or before the controlling operative unit ends. Avoid duplicating identical quotes or dumping unrelated whole-summary text. Keep excerpt/format diagnostics separate from substantive rulings.\n\nAnswer every question including every requested part. Save valid JSON with top-level reader, inputs_read, delivery_receipt, source_unit_checks and answers. Each answer must contain id, clauses, operative_quotes (complete relevant units), answer (concise direct case ruling/calculation), support (supported/partial/unsupported) and evidence (summary section references). Every substantive same-entry field is assessed; do not give contradictory unsupported caveats for a ruling you have resolved. Do not evaluate or edit the summary.\n'''
protocol_version=sys.argv[3] if len(sys.argv)>3 else 'v1'
if protocol_version in ['v2','v3','v4','v5']:
 base=base.replace('select the complete relevant operative units; then give concise direct rulings for each clause and actual calculated values in numeric cases.', 'select complete relevant operative units; then give concise direct rulings for each clause. For each concrete case explicitly name the resulting actor and case outcome, and supply the actual calculations the question asks. Do not stop at a general selection rule or formula when a case conclusion is requested.')
 base=base.replace('Source-unit integrity: choose complete heading-bounded leaf subsections or explicit unions of complete relevant paragraphs/lists, or a full relevant table row with header and governing context.', 'Source-unit integrity v2: mechanically choose complete governing heading units, not arbitrary paragraph excerpts. Index Markdown headings and take each relevant level-2 or level-3 unit from its heading through the next heading of the same or higher level, retaining ALL paragraphs, peer steps and child details. A union of complete relevant leaf units is permitted. Include controlling parent introductions and earlier definitions when they supply an asked fact. Do not select only the first paragraph of a multi-paragraph procedure.')
 base=base.replace('For prose keep actual complete paragraph/list boundaries.', 'For prose, verify each selected span begins at the chosen heading and ends at its next same-or-higher heading, allowing only boundary whitespace trimming. For procedural questions check every asked step, destination, timing and exception against the entire selected unit. For table rows keep the full actual row and header plus the complete governing procedural context.')
if protocol_version in ['v3','v4','v5']:
 base=base.replace('For each concrete case explicitly name the resulting actor and case outcome, and supply the actual calculations the question asks.', 'For each concrete case explicitly name the resulting actor and case outcome, and supply the actual calculations the question asks. If multiple participants or items have requested amounts/outcomes, give a row for every requested participant/item and a column for every asked result; fill every cell, including zero or no-change results when those are the actual answers. For question-specified changes, track each original object exactly once through any additions, removals or replacements before stating the final state; do not count the same remaining object twice under different descriptions.')
 base=base.replace('Each answer must contain id, clauses, operative_quotes (complete relevant units), answer (concise direct case ruling/calculation), support (supported/partial/unsupported) and evidence (summary section references).', 'Each answer must contain id, clauses, operative_quotes (complete relevant units), answer (concise direct case ruling/calculation), support (supported/partial/unsupported) and evidence (summary section references). The clauses field must be an array of objects with the question clause, an explicit ruling for that clause, and its operative-unit references; a list of labels alone is not sufficient. Include requested participant/item outcomes in those rulings, and self-check each actual asked clause before saving. Use only scenario facts and frozen-summary rules, never invented quantities or participants.')
if protocol_version in ['v4','v5']:
 base += '''\nMechanical self-check v4: For every requested numeric output, write the expression using the question's inputs and the selected rule, evaluate it, and independently check that your final answer uses that exact result. For questions that change named objects, give a before/change/after inventory with distinct neutral object IDs, each original object appearing once. Then identify which surviving objects are affected by the next rule and which are not, with the rule-based reason. Verify that every object mentioned in your final prose exists in that inventory and that no object is both affected and unaffected by the same event. These checks must be recorded in each applicable answer's case_check field; use not_applicable for a pure lookup question. Before saving, independently compare every clause ruling and final answer against these calculations/inventories and the complete operative quotes, fixing any contradiction. Preserve full direct rulings rather than using a generic assertion that checks passed.\n\nDelivery offsets must be Unicode character offsets: use read_text() and string slicing, not byte slicing or wc -c. Report the UTF-8 file hash separately from Unicode character counts.\n'''
if protocol_version=='v5':
 base += '''\nStructured-result rendering v5: In every numeric or state-changing case, first create and verify one structured result from the case_check calculation/inventory. Include clearly labeled requested amounts/outcomes, the actual final inventory, and which surviving objects the next rule affects, as applicable. Use that SAME verified result object (or the directly relevant subobject) as each clause ruling and as the answer, assigning it programmatically when writing JSON. Structured objects/tables are valid direct rulings. Do not independently paraphrase a checked state or number in additional prose: redundant handwritten restatements can contradict an otherwise correct check. Keep necessary timing/eligibility/source-limit conclusions in the shared result too, rather than dropping them. For pure lookup questions a concise text ruling is fine. Before saving, mechanically confirm that every repeated result field equals its verified structured source. All substantive fields will still be graded, including checks and clauses.\n'''
if protocol_version in ['v6','v7','v8']:
 base='''You are an independent rules-summary reader in a blind evaluation. Read ONLY these two rules-data files:
{summary}
{questions}
Write ONLY {output}.
Do not read sources, answer keys, manifests, earlier answers/grades/reviews, other files, parent history, chats, agent/runtime metadata or web links. Do not browse, use prior game knowledge, communicate with other readers, or evaluate/edit the summary. The summary is your sole rules authority.

Deliver EVERY character of BOTH inputs before answering. Use read_text() and contiguous Unicode string slices <=5000 characters, with one separate model-visible tool result per slice and cap >=4000 tokens. Print file path, character start/end/total, chunk SHA256 and exact full text. Separately hash the UTF-8 file bytes. Preserve complete delivery_receipt ranges/hashes in your output. Recover any truncated range in smaller pieces; do not rely on line counts, byte offsets, silent loading or cropped output.

For each question independently:
1. Enumerate every actually requested clause. Treat the stated scenario as given; do not reject a hypothetical merely because the summary does not narrate it.
2. Search the whole summary for every relevant item and term. Read the complete governing units and controlling earlier definitions before declaring anything absent. If a requested rule is absent or expressly unspecified, state the exact limit and never invent an official ruling.
3. Separate stated case facts, rule-based consequences and unspecified facts. Preserve all stated role/eligibility constraints. Do not arbitrarily assign an unspecified owner, value, participant, sequence, role or outcome. Keep it unidentified or conditional when necessary; do not fill unknowns merely to complete a table or inventory.
4. Give direct decisions for every asked clause. Concrete cases need actual resulting actors/objects/outcomes and requested numeric results, rather than only a selection rule or formula. For multiple requested participants/results, provide labeled rows/columns including requested zero/no-change outcomes. Calculate the requested total as well as any useful components, with an evaluated expression.
5. Check only the facts and transformations needed to answer the question. For an explicit state change, track the stated original objects once through removal/replacement/addition, then identify affected surviving objects. Use neutral IDs and preserve unspecified attributes. Do not construct extra hypothetical ownerships, rolls or events. A pure permission/lookup question needs no invented initial/final case.
6. Reuse the verified structured result programmatically in the answer and relevant clause rulings rather than independently paraphrasing checked numbers/states. Structured objects/tables are valid direct rulings. Retain all asked timing, eligibility, destination and source-limit conclusions. Do not add redundant prose that can contradict the checked result.

Source-unit integrity: mechanically index Markdown headings. For each relevant level-2 or level-3 unit, quote its heading and ALL content through the next heading of the same or higher level, including child details, peer steps and exceptions. A union of complete relevant leaf units is permitted. Include controlling parent introductions/earlier definitions when needed. Do not crop the first paragraph of a multi-paragraph procedure. Keep full actual table rows, all cells, header/legend and governing context. Before saving, verify each quote is verbatim and complete at its true heading boundary, allowing only boundary whitespace trimming. Avoid unrelated whole-summary dumping and duplicate quotes.

Save valid JSON with top-level reader, inputs_read, delivery_receipt, source_unit_checks and answers. There must be exactly one answer for every question. Each entry must contain id, clauses, operative_quotes, answer, support, evidence and case_check. clauses is an array of objects containing the requested clause, a direct ruling, and operative-unit references; labels alone are insufficient. operative_quotes contains the complete selected units. support is supported/partial/unsupported; evidence names summary sections. case_check records minimal stated inputs and the needed evaluated calculation or explicit state update, or not_applicable for pure lookup. Do not populate checks with assumptions or additional case facts not established by the question/rules.

Before saving, independently compare every asked clause, answer, clause ruling and case_check against the question's exact givens and full selected rules. Verify all requested results are present and consistent; each asserted case fact must be a stated fact or a justified consequence, with unknowns preserved. Mechanically verify repeated structured results match their shared source. All substantive same-entry fields will be graded, so an unasked invented detail or contradictory caveat can invalidate an otherwise correct answer. Complete same-entry quotations may supply ordinary lookup rules; actual case results/calculations must still be resolved. Keep format diagnostics separate from factual rulings.
'''
if protocol_version=='v7':
 base += '''\nUse this exact generic rendering function when constructing EVERY answer. It supplies no game facts; you independently derive checked_result, checked_inputs and the complete quotations from the permitted files. Set checked_inputs to minimal literal givens and justified calculations, preserving unknowns. Put all asked conclusions in checked_result. Do not invent concrete inputs to evaluate a quantity whose needed inputs are unspecified. Clause references enumerate the actual asked clauses and governing units. Call the function in your writing code; do not hand-author or subsequently overwrite answer/ruling/case_check result copies. This mechanically enforces the shared-result method rather than relying on an assertion that separate prose agrees.\n\n```python\nfrom copy import deepcopy\n\ndef render_answer(question_id, clause_refs, checked_result, operative_quotes, support, evidence, checked_inputs="not_applicable"):\n    entry = dict(\n        id=question_id,\n        clauses=[dict(clause=c["clause"], ruling=deepcopy(checked_result), operative_unit_refs=c["operative_unit_refs"]) for c in clause_refs],\n        operative_quotes=operative_quotes,\n        answer=deepcopy(checked_result),\n        support=support,\n        evidence=evidence,\n        case_check=dict(checked_inputs=checked_inputs, checked_result=deepcopy(checked_result)),\n    )\n    assert entry["answer"] == entry["case_check"]["checked_result"]\n    assert all(c["ruling"] == entry["answer"] for c in entry["clauses"])\n    return entry\n```\n\nFor each question verify the checked_result itself against the exact question and full rules before passing it to the function. The helper does not establish correctness or permit omitted asked facts. All checked_inputs and result contents remain subject to strict factual grading. Save the rendered entries as the answers array with the required top-level receipts and source checks.\n'''
if protocol_version=='v8':
 base += '''\nConcrete-decision rendering v8: Classify each question as pure lookup or application of stated case givens. Use checked_inputs="not_applicable" ONLY for pure lookup. For a case, first write a case_decisions array resolving EVERY requested case outcome. Each item needs clause and case_outcome; include the actual named participants/items and selected results when determined by the givens. Where a selection matters, explicitly name the affected objects and relevant exclusions rather than only quoting the selection rule. Preserve genuine unknowns and source limits; never invent unspecified attributes. A general statement that an event can/may happen, or to act if it happens, does not resolve whether it DOES happen in the supplied case. Give the determined case decision first, then any useful general explanation.\n\nUse this exact fact-free rendering helper for EVERY entry. Independently derive checked_result, minimal checked_inputs, case_decisions and complete quotations from the allowed files. For cases, the helper requires explicit decision records and carries them into all repeated result fields. It supplies no game facts and does not establish whether your decisions are correct. Do not hand-author or subsequently overwrite the rendered result copies. All substantive fields remain strictly graded.\n\n```python\nfrom copy import deepcopy\n\ndef render_answer(question_id, clause_refs, checked_result, operative_quotes, support, evidence, checked_inputs="not_applicable", case_decisions=None):\n    if checked_inputs != "not_applicable":\n        assert isinstance(case_decisions, list) and case_decisions\n        assert all(d.get("clause") and d.get("case_outcome") for d in case_decisions)\n    if case_decisions:\n        checked_result = dict(explanation=deepcopy(checked_result), case_decisions=deepcopy(case_decisions))\n    entry = dict(\n        id=question_id,\n        clauses=[dict(clause=c["clause"], ruling=deepcopy(checked_result), operative_unit_refs=c["operative_unit_refs"]) for c in clause_refs],\n        operative_quotes=operative_quotes,\n        answer=deepcopy(checked_result),\n        support=support,\n        evidence=evidence,\n        case_check=dict(checked_inputs=checked_inputs, checked_result=deepcopy(checked_result)),\n    )\n    assert entry["answer"] == entry["case_check"]["checked_result"]\n    assert all(c["ruling"] == entry["answer"] for c in entry["clauses"])\n    return entry\n```\n\nBefore calling the helper, verify each case_outcome against the exact current question and full governing source units. Do not borrow givens from other questions, leave a determined outcome conditional, or replace a requested concrete decision with a general rule. Save all rendered entries and the required top-level receipts/source checks.\n'''
manifest['protocol_version']=protocol_version
for label in ['a','b']:
 prompt=base.format(summary=D/'summary-snapshot.md',questions=D/'questions.json',output=D/f'reader-{label}.json')
 (D/f'reader-{label}-prompt.txt').write_text(prompt)
manifest['prompt_hashes']={l:h(D/f'reader-{l}-prompt.txt') for l in ['a','b']}
(D/'input-manifest.json').write_text(json.dumps(manifest,indent=2)+'\n')
p=json.loads((R/'progress.json').read_text());p['phase']=name;p['iterations'].append({'name':name,'question_count':len(json.loads((D/'questions.json').read_text())['questions']),'status':'frozen'});(R/'progress.json').write_text(json.dumps(p,indent=2)+'\n')
